course: dictionary
lesson: 2549
title: What a definition tells you
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A definition is a short explanation of what a word or idea means. «A definition is a short explanation of what a word means» is the kind of sentence you find in a dictionary. When you want to be sure what a word means, look for its definition.
explain: Definition has more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one. «The definition on the new TV was so sharp you could count the leaves on the trees.» Here definition means how clear a picture is, not what a word means. Ask yourself: is this sentence about a meaning, a picture, or a shape?
explain: In maths, a definition says exactly what a thing is. A square is a rectangle with four equal sides. Philosophers such as Socrates tested definitions with examples that broke them, to see whether a definition was really good.
explain: «By definition, a square has four equal sides» means because of what the word means. The phrase «the definition of» is often followed by the meaning itself, so read on to find the explanation.
fact: A definition is a statement of what a word or idea means.
fact: «Definition» can also mean how clear a picture or sound is, as in «high definition» or HD.
fact: «Definition» can also mean a clear shape or outline, as in «muscle definition».
fact: «By definition» means because of what the word means.
fact: Scientists sometimes argue about definitions: since 2006 astronomers have called Pluto a dwarf planet, though some still argue about the definition.
exercise: «A definition is a short explanation of what a word means.» What is a definition? | *A statement of what a word or idea means | A rule for playing a game | A picture on a screen | A short poem
exercise: «The definition on the new TV was so sharp I could count the leaves.» What does definition mean here? | *How clear a picture is | A kind of sharp knife | A statement of what a word means | A rule for the game
exercise: «His arms showed clear muscle definition after months of training.» What does definition mean in this sentence? | *A clear shape or outline | Lots of muscle, very heavy | A kind of sport | A weak and tired feeling
test: «By definition, a square has four equal sides.» What does by definition mean? | *Because of what the word means | Only sometimes | By accident, without thinking | Next to the house
test: Which sentence gives a definition of a rectangle? | Rectangles are my favourite colour | Rectangles are fun to draw | *A rectangle is a four-sided shape with four right angles | Rectangles are very long
exam: Socrates tested definitions with examples that broke them. What was he trying to find out? | How to build a clock | *Whether a definition was really good | How many words a child knows | Where the Greek words came from
